  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+1).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14246608/assets/902c8394181aefb301c901b3792e89e909ba36ecba3a9b8113fc42b80fd08870.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ increases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{log}_{5}⁡(x+1)=\\infty \n$$",
